              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Sanskrit for a burning feeling, then the Sanskrit for runs a fever."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: वेदना",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "वेदना — vedanā — \"agony; acute pain\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "रात्रौ मम दन्ते वेदना अभवत्। rātrau mama dante vedanā abhavat. In the night I had a terrible toothache."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A feminine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "वेदना (vedanā) comes from the root √vid, \"to know, to feel\": what is felt; MW gives \"pain, torture, agony\" (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
